This Python module assigns a spending category to a merchant name.

To categorize a merchant:
    compare the merchant name, ignoring case:
        contains "grocery" or "market"              | groceries
        contains "gas" or "fuel"                    | transport
        contains "cafe" or "restaurant" or "pizza"  | eating out
        contains "pharmacy"                         | health
        anything else                               | other

For example, categorizing "Metro Grocery" must give "groceries".
Categorizing "Green Fuel Stop" must give "transport".
Categorizing "LUIGI PIZZA" must give "eating out".
Categorizing "Book Nook" must give "other".
